# S-12 HIGH-POWER BASELINE PROBE.  NOT a delta-debug rung -- an INSTRUMENT.
#
# Why this file exists: every S-12 arm-vs-baseline comparison so far scored a 1-bit,
# ~8-minute draw (wedge or return) against a baseline whose wedge rate in the SAME slot
# configuration is measured at 1 wedge in 2 valid draws, not the 0.94 that was borrowed
# from a DIFFERENT slot configuration.  At that rate five draws cannot separate a cured
# arm from a lucky one: 7/7 returns against a 1-in-2 baseline is Fisher p ~= 0.22.
#
# The fix is not more draws, it is more prepares per draw.  If the per-prepare wedge
# probability is p, a file with N independent depth-2 prepares wedges with probability
# 1-(1-p)^N -- ~0.998 at N=120 even for p as low as 0.05.  So a boot that COMPLETES this
# file is strong evidence the arm is cured, and a boot that wedges is the expected
# baseline behaviour rather than a coin flip.
#
# Design constraints, each of which has burned a run before:
#   * Every table is EMPTY.  S-12 fires in sqlite3WhereCodeOneLoopStart at PREPARE time,
#     with no rows processed -- adding rows would test the wrong path and cost runtime.
#   * Every query is a BARE two-table cartesian join, byte-for-byte the shape of the
#     dd2_join rung that wedges, and NOT the WHERE-qualified shape: an equality predicate
#     makes the planner build an automatic covering index and a Bloom filter, which is a
#     DIFFERENT codegen path.  Checked with EXPLAIN QUERY PLAN -- the bare join gives the
#     two plain SCANs that dd2_join gives, the qualified one does not.
#   * Every query TEXT is distinct.  sqlite3_prepare_v2 has no cross-call statement cache,
#     so this is belt-and-braces, but a shared text is exactly the kind of silent
#     deduplication that would turn 120 prepares into 1 and make a clean run meaningless.
#   * Expected result sets are EMPTY, so a completed run reports query_pass=120 and any
#     nonzero query_fail means the instrument, not the silicon, needs looking at.
#
# POSITIVE CONTROL: this file must wedge the unmodified baseline on silicon.  If it does
# not, it is not a probe for anything and no arm result taken with it may be believed.

statement ok
CREATE TABLE s0(a INTEGER, b INTEGER, c INTEGER, d INTEGER, e INTEGER)

statement ok
